            "review_title": "Review at Hoi An Coffee House",
            "review_text": "Peter A\nBangkok, Thailand62 contributions\n0\nNot Where I Intended to Go But A Pleasant Surprise\nDec 2018 • Solo\nHai An Coffee House is tucked away in a side alley off a street of trendy shops in HCMC. Facing the storefronts, the alley is to the left of RAP (a clothing store), which opens up to a courtyard having the entrance of an apartment, a clothing and gift shop and the café. There is also a street food cart parked at wall to the right of the café.\n\nHai An is a quaint place with a small porch area if you care to sit outdoors and two connecting rooms; one with regular tables and chairs, and one with raised tables with stools. There is a counter against the front windows with stools you can sit and plug in a laptop or mobile phone. They have WI-FI and with the décor and easy Viet music creates a very nice atmosphere to work or chat with friends or eat a meal. Staff was very friendly and spoke good English.\n\nThe beverage menu includes Vietnamese-style coffee, both iced and hot, along with teas, smoothies, juices, etc. The food menu had approx. nine hot dishes (pictures on the wall, framed along with the artwork. I had the Stir Fried Rice-noodles with beef and if was quite good, along with a fresh coconut drink.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten December 15, 2018",
